 <td width="100%" height="25" background="http://www.geocities.com/hobbeslobber/images/back3.gif" colspan="2"><p align="center"><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif" color="#dddddd" size="2"><a href="http://www.geocities.com/hobbeslobber/">Bobbins Rumblebelly</a> | Football-shaped Druid of the <font color="orange">41</font>st Level | Officer, <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/GSheldon">Defenders of the Faith</A> | Rodcet Nife <BR></p></font>

 </td>
<tr>

</TABLE><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#f7f5e6><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/usneakyguy.showPublicProfile>sneakyguy</A></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Global user</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>7/1/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>11:13:55 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Re: LOL, I don't know about 34, but druids kick shaman *** before then.</font></B><HR><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">first, shamans and druids DD superiority rotates every spell set starting at 14,<br>
<br>
so... at lvl 14, 24, 34, and 44 shamans have better dd than druids,<br>
<br>
druids solo better than shaman UNTIL lvl 34.. at that point, a shaman can solo til lvl 50<br>
<br>
shamans dots are better, so any druid that doesnt have his head up his arse, will know that a shamans dots are indeed better than a druids (although my shaman did feel inferior when he did not get a dot at 14.. whereas my druid got stinging swarm at 14)<br>
<br>
shamans buffs are better, best str buffs in game (at lower lvls druids win this.. but like u said.. at low lvls stat buffs mean nothing :), sta buffs give hit points, agi buffs give ac, ac buffs, and we get &quot;real&quot; (lol@innerfire) hit point buffs later as well--druids do have better hit point buffs however<br>
<br>
shamans take the de-buff area, malise line, tagar line, disempower line -- although that is mainly a pvp kinda spell lol<br>
<br>
shaman have the quickness spells, pet spells,and FRENZY line.. coupled with regen spell... frenzy (especially for troll) can kick major arse<br>
<br>
druids-- have harmony, snare, teleports, dmg shields, great DD at high lvls, and actually get GOOD spells post 50 (unlike shaman)<br>
<br>
pvp--shaman after lvl 44 have no competition unless its a necro.. or possibly mage, druids can still kick butt at pvp tho, specially vs a melee class<br>
<br>
overall both classes rule, play what u like, and dont bash shaman--u may get a warhammer to the head one day</font><P><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#e6ebd7><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/udienia.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Dienia</A></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Registered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>7/5/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>2:11:45 pm</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Ya, but what race of Druid/Shaman?</font></B><HR><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">I'm playing a Barbarian Shaman, and a half elf Druid.  Imho, half-elves are very hard to level.  I got up to lvl 9 with my Druid and am STUCK.  I started up a Barb Shaman and while I'm still at level 6, I'm having a darn good time.  Blackburrow is not as big a death trap for me at lvl 6 as it was for my half elf at level 6.<br>
<br>
I really do enjoy Druids but am so frustrated with my half-elf.  I admit, I also have a grudge because Dienia gets hit on constantly simply because Verant and Sony must have thought it fun to leave female half elves' chest and rear end exposed for the world to view, no matter what I put on her for clothing or armor. Getting &quot;hey baby&quot; all the time when looking for a group gets pretty old to the point where it's rare for me to group with any males at all.  I've got some great friends for grouping, but it's hard for us to get together.<br>
<br>
Any recommendations for which races to play as a Druid, if so, please state WHY.  I have heard halfling is best, any thoughts on this?</font><P><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#f7f5e6><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/uvigganglambane.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Viggan Glambane</A>&nbsp; <IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/image/globalBlack.gif BORDER=0 WIDTH=10 HEIGHT=10></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Registered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>7/13/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>8:42:04 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Re: Ya, but what race of Druid/Shaman?</font></B><HR><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">I think shaman and druid are pretty comparable class, at least to the point that they compete for the same spots in groups many times. Power-wise, I think druids have a better suit of spells for solo play while shaman and druids are about equal for group desirablility (evac vs. debuffs?).<br>
<br>
Shaman do get very nice class armor quests and generally can melee more, but druid damage shields and higher base wisdom seem to even this out. <br>
<br>
Best race for a druid? Wood Elf or halfling. I think haflings are cooler, but I prefer woodelves for their higher base charisma. I use charm animal a LOT. <br>
<br>
All in all, I think every class is pretty good if you can play around their failings. Even wizards, which I consider the most useless class in the game, can be good if played well. My druid can do a ton of damage in a fight with damage shields alone, a fact that many over look.</font><P>Viggan Glambane<BR>
39th Level Dwarven Rogue<BR>
Pacal Sidhe<BR>
25th Level Wood Elf Druid<BR>
Prexus<BR><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#e6ebd7><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/ugoonster.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Goonster</A>&nbsp; <IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/ezgfx/gicons/anim_1.gif BORDER=0 WIDTH=10 HEIGHT=10></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Registered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>7/24/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>8:47:23 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT><BR><img src=http://goonster.bizland.com/web/wolf.gif WIDTH=60 HEIGHT=60></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Re: Ya, but what race of Druid/Shaman?</font></B><HR><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Yada Yada Yada... Being a Druid myself, I will hang my head in shame and tell you that Shamans, at high levels (which is where it counts) are stronger group members than us. How many raids have you been on where a Druid is picked over a Shaman?... that's what I thought. When you think about it, who cares who can kill who in a duel, who is more powerful, who is more mana-efficient. Who gets picked first to go on raids? That's right, the Shaman, every time. Druids get picked, only if there is one spot left and there is absolutely nobody else around to fill it, or you &quot;KNOW&quot; somebody who can get you in.<br>
<br>
But I'm not bitter, I have a steady group of friends, consisting of:<br>
<br>
Druid(me)<br>
Shaman<br>
Warrior(x2)<br>
Enchanter<br>
Cleric<br>
<br>
We do our own thing, and we may not be the EQ &quot;Perfect Group&quot; poster child, but let me tell you, we got our game screwed on tight. We are all good friends and have a great time when we are together. So maybe we should all stop bickering and arguing over what class is strongest and just get out there and kick some a$$.<br>
<br>
Goonster Sportinwood<br>
42 Halfling/Druid<br>
<br>
&quot;When in doubt, add commas.&quot;</font><P><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#f7f5e6><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/uvigganglambane.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Viggan Glambane</A>&nbsp; <IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/image/globalBlack.gif BORDER=0 WIDTH=10 HEIGHT=10></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Registered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>7/24/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>11:33:14 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Re: Ya, but what race of Druid/Shaman?</font></B><HR><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Shaman v. druid for a group slot? It depends on the situation. Flat out, a shaman will be able to unload more damage at a given level and debuff better than an enchanter. But, evacs and teleports are vital in the mid to high range dungeons, and a druid is a LOT more survivable than a wizard. <br>
<br>
Planes raids? Who knows? I'm not in an uber guild so the odds are slim that any of my characters will hit the planes. Since a lot of the kunark loot is better, no loss IMO. <br>
<br>
My personal opinion is that the following classes are vital for a balanced group from 30-50: warrior, cleric, enchanter and druid. These four classes give you the lion's share of the most important capabilities in the game:<br>
<br>
- tanking/taunting/pulling<br>
- crowd control<br>
- debuffs (resists, stats, attack speed and movement speed)<br>
- buffs (hp, ac, str, resists, attack speed, movement speed)<br>
- healing, resurrection<br>
- mana/hp regen<br>
- damage shields<br>
- evac/teleport<br>
- DoTs, DD and stuns<br>
- all varieties of invis<br>
<br>
I prefer to fill my remaining two spots with either 2 more pure melee (rogue &amp; monk) or one more pure melee and shaman. <br>
<br>
If you look at all the capabilities of a group with 2 tanks, 1 cleric, 1 shaman, 1 enchanter and 1 druid it is simply awesome. The shaman, druid, and enchanter overlap so many other classes' capabilities that they become greater than the sum. This group is supremely flexible.<br>
<br>
Fire resistant mobs? NP, the shaman nukes and the druid and cleric heal and dmg shield. Undead? NP, the cleric nukes while the shaman and druid handle heals. Bad pull? no worries, you have mez or evac. Dungeon too crowded, not a problem just teleport somewhere else. <br>
<br>
So imo, a druid is a key element of a group. Plus you get the added benefit of being able to solo if ya want to. <br>
</font><P>Viggan Glambane<BR>
39th Level Dwarven Rogue<BR>
Pacal Sidhe<BR>
25th Level Wood Elf Druid<BR>
Prexus<BR><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#e6ebd7><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/ugoonster.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Goonster</A>&nbsp; <IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/ezgfx/gicons/anim_1.gif BORDER=0 WIDTH=10 HEIGHT=10></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Registered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>7/25/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>3:31:02 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT><BR><img src=http://goonster.bizland.com/web/wolf.gif WIDTH=60 HEIGHT=60></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Re: Ya, but what race of Druid/Shaman?</font></B><HR><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Bah, solo shmolo, soloing sucks.<br>
And BTW, you dont ever, ever, ever EVAC from the plains. If you EVAC or GATE, you will be black listed for sure.<br>
<br>
Goonster Sportinwood<br>
42 Halfling/Druid/Tunare<br>
<br>
&quot;When in doubt, add commas.&quot;</font><P><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#f7f5e6><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/uvigganglambane.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Viggan Glambane</A>&nbsp; <IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/image/globalBlack.gif BORDER=0 WIDTH=10 HEIGHT=10></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Registered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>7/25/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>6:30:01 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Re: Ya, but what race of Druid/Shaman?</font></B><HR><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">I'm not talking about the planes. The group I described is geared toward the average, everyday zones where a single group can operate effectively. <br>
<br>
Multigroup raids are an entirely different animal. Prior to the level cap increase, multiple groups were the only way to handle planes/dragon raids. </font><P>Viggan Glambane<BR>
39th Level Dwarven Rogue<BR>
Pacal Sidhe<BR>
27th Level Wood Elf Druid<BR>
Prexus<BR><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#e6ebd7><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/uginslunger.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Ginslunger</A></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Registered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>7/27/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>5:33:01 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Re: Ya, but what race of Druid/Shaman?</font></B><HR><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Nice to read a different point of view.  I must say that although I play a shaman, I really like the info on these boards.<br>
<br>
To me, the critical members of a group are warrior/pally, cleric and enchanter.  Then it gets a little fuzzy.  If a wizard is present for evac, I'd personally lean toward a shaman.  If not, I'd prefer a druid and magician combo.  Either are viable.  I think shamen are more group friendly, but the druid evac ability would sometimes sway me into choosing a druid over a shaman.  It also depends upon the spawn.  If crowd control is needed for pulls, my first choice would be a feign-pulling monk as the sixth member of the group.  If not available, a druid is need to fulfill this role.<br>
<br>
With the discussion about feign-pulling being nerfed, I can definitely see druids becoming more popular in groups.<br>
<br>
Eventhough I'm a capable soloer, druids win the solo ability hands down.<br>
<br>
I think the two classes, while very comparable, have the unfair onus put one them that a group needs one or the other, but not both.  Let's try to get that changed!  Especially at higher levels, our classes diverge somewhat into different abilities.  Post lvl 24, having both a druid and a shaman in a group would be advantageous.<br>
<br>
Ginslunger<br>
29 Shaman<br>
Torvonnilous</font><P><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#f7f5e6><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/ugilliongiladion.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Gillion Giladion</A></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Registered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>8/21/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>11:08:10 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Shamans are at least as powerful as Druids</font></B><HR><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">I'm not sure what the original poster's point was, but having played a Barb Shaman out to L37 I have to say that he clearly doesn't understand the Shaman class very well.<br>
<br>
It's true that early on Druids can handle full camps using Harmony that a Shaman couldn't hope to break.<br>
<br>
It's also true that early on one-on-one in casting assisted melee Shamans can handle wandering mobs in 90 seconds that Druids would have trouble kiting over 10 minutes.<br>
<br>
At L13 my Druid used Harmony and Snare along with Shield of Thistles to camp the river Bandits in North Karana.  It took me about 4-5 hours to make 14.<br>
<br>
At L13 my Shaman used Drowsy, his Banded Armor (AC was nearly 70 points higher than the Druid), his STR/AGI/DEX buffs and SoW (5 levels earlier than Druid) along with his Poison DoT and Frost Rift to solo Scarecrows in West Karana.  It took him 4-5 hours to get 14.<br>
<br>
They were EQUAL in power at L13.  From 9-13 I would say that overall the Shaman was more powerful due to the earlier acquisition of SoW.<br>
<br>
At L35 my Shaman was soloing HG's, kiting all the while AFTER the DoT reduction.  At L35 he was excellent in a group.<br>
<br>
I'm hoping that the Druid will stay true to form and be as powerful at 35 as the Shaman was.<br>
<br>
I've now played Shaman to 37, Cleric to 32 and Druid to 15 and to be honest I see NO difference in terms of real power between the 3 classes.  Clerics are the most powerful in a group.  Shamans are very strong solo and still good in a group and I'm expecting to find the same holds true for Druids.<br>
<br>
At least I hope so.</font><P><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#e6ebd7><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/udienia.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Dienia</A></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Registered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>8/29/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>11:39:01 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">Druid vs. Shaman</font></B><HR><FONT SIZE=2 FACE="Verdana,Arial">I ended up starting a Barbarian Shaman.  I leveled her much faster than the half-elf druid, and got her past 9.  The Barbarian Shaman does solo quite well, and is great in groups.  The only problem with grouping is that I must very clearly define what I'll do for group members and see what they need from me as most times that I've grouped, members expect me to tank, buff, heal and cast DoT's.  There's never enough mana to do all that.  At the early levels, I don't feel the Druid can solo as well. <br>
<br>
I deleted the half-elf druid and have started over with a halfling druid.  I think being a half elf was a big part of the problem in leveling the druid.  Note that many people (including eqdruids) feel that half-elves are the worst for the druid class.  <br>
<br>
Both classes are great, but since the spells they have fall into differnt categories (DoT versus DD) I think comparing them is a bit difficult.  The shamans start out with much better buffs, and frankly, the Disempower spell a shammie gets at 14 rocks as it lowers stats in most areas on the opponent, making it easier to melee. <br>
<br>
Right now, if I had to pick just class, I'd take a shaman any day.  We get better buffs at the outset, and all the races that can be shaman are phsyically strong too, in addition to Shaman having more options for what armor they wear.<br>
<br>
</font><P><P><i></i></TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE BORDER=0 WIDTH=95%><TR><TD ALIGN=LEFT></TD><TD ALIGN=RIGHT><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.showMessage?topicID=144.topic><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1><< Prev Topic</FONT></A> &nbsp;<A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.showMessage?topicID=128.topic><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Next Topic >></FONT></A> </TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE WIDTH=95% BORDER=0><TR><TD><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.showAddReplyScreenFromWeb?topicID=89.topic&index=17><IMG SRC=http://www.execpc.com/~msippel/thedruidsgrove/images/addreply.gif border=0></A></TD><TD><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.emailToFriend?topicID=89.topic><IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/images/email.gif BORDER=0 ALT="Email This To a Friend"></A><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>&nbsp;Email This To a Friend</FONT><BR><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.threadControl?topicID=89.topic><IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/gfx/deleteThread.gif BORDER=0 ALT="Topic Control Image"></A><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;Topic Commands (Moderator only)</FONT><BR><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.subscribeUnregisteredToTopic?topicID=89.topic><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Subscribe</FONT></A>  <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Click to receive email notification of replies</FONT><BR><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.unsubscribeUnregisteredToTopic?topicID=89.topic><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Unsubscribe</FONT></A>  <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Click to stop receiving email notification of replies</FONT><BR></TD><TD></TD></TR><TR><TD COLSPAN=3 ALIGN=CENTER><BR><FORM ACTION=http://pub2.ezboard.com/BBSForum.jumpShowForum METHOD=POST><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Jump to: </FONT><SELECT NAME=forumName><OPTION VALUE=thedruidsgrovegeneral>Genera